### star-code-architect/SKILL.md
--- 1
5. **Verify per group; delegate where it helps.** Delegate surveys and migrations wherever it helps: hand off a bounded, independent area or migration group whenever collaboration tools are available and delegation materially helps, and execute locally when it does not. When delegating, dispatch a read-only sub-agent for a read-only survey — on the READ tier's model (conventions §10.8), where the harness can name one — or a writing sub-agent for a migration, on the EXEC tier's model, and give it the narrow brief in `references/orchestration_spec.md`; a migration agent writes only its own group's files. Either way: disjoint file ownership per group, re-run every check yourself (never trust a self-reported pass; a migration's checks are cheap, so this skill does not take conventions §6.3's evidence-acceptance route), commit once per verified group, retry ≤2, restore what still fails.
+++ 1
5. **The main agent orchestrates and verifies; subagents execute.** Surveys go to read-only `Agent` subagents (`subagent_type: Explore`, `model:` the READ tier value read from `.env`, omitted when that key is empty); migrations go to `Agent` subagents (`subagent_type: general-purpose`, `model:` the EXEC tier value read from `.env`, omitted when that key is empty) whose writes are limited to their own group's files. Both carry disjoint file ownership and structured returns. The main agent re-runs every check itself (never trusts a self-reported pass; a migration's checks are cheap, so this skill does not take conventions §6.3's evidence-acceptance route), commits once per verified group, retries ≤2, and restores what still fails. Spec: `references/orchestration_spec.md`.
